---
kind: lore
id: lore.places
title: What you find when nobody is there
---

<entry id="libraryClosedSunday" on="placeVisit" target="place.library" category="bark" priority="5" when="@sunday">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: A card in the door, in careful capitals: CLOSED SUNDAYS. BOOKS MAY BE RETURNED THROUGH THE SLOT. PLEASE DO NOT RETURN FISH.
</entry>

<entry id="libraryShut" on="placeVisit" target="place.library" category="bark" when="!@sunday && !holds('present', ['ines', 'library'])">
  <match on="run.slot">
    <when is="morning">
      @narrator{code="0010"}: The library doesn't open until one. Through the glass you can see a returns trolley and a sleeping cat.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @narrator{code="0020"}: The library is dark. Someone has left a desk lamp on over a stack of paper samples.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>

<entry id="pierEmpty" on="placeVisit" target="place.pier" category="bark" when="!holds('present', ['theo', 'pier'])">
  <match on="run.slot">
    <when is="night">
      @narrator{code="0010"}: The pier at night is all creak and slap. Theo's nets are folded under a tarpaulin, weighed down with a brick.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @narrator{code="0020"}: The boats are out. The reed beds rustle behind the pier with nobody cutting them.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</entry>

<entry id="lighthouseShut" on="placeVisit" target="place.lighthouse" category="bark" when="!holds('present', ['theo', 'lighthouse'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The lighthouse door is padlocked. A tide table is taped to the inside of the glass, one date circled in biro.
</entry>

<entry id="squareQuiet" on="placeVisit" target="place.square" category="bark">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: Gulls, a bench, a war memorial with fresh flowers. The square is waiting for something.
</entry>

<entry id="shopBark" on="placeVisit" target="place.shop" category="bark" when="holds('present', ['pell', 'shop'])">
  @pell{code="0010"}: Back already? The glue's where it always is.
</entry>

<beat id="theoBark" on="placeVisit" target="place.pier" when="holds('present', ['theo', 'pier'])" once="false">
  ::set{run.seen.theo = run.day}
  <match on="run.aff.theo">
    <when is="3..">
      @theo{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: Qualified hands! Come to watch me untangle things?
    </when>
    <when is="..0">
      @theo{code="0020" emotion="neutral"}: Busy.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @theo{code="0030"}: Tide's turning. Mind the nets.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>

<beat id="inesBark" on="placeVisit" target="place.library" when="holds('present', ['ines', 'library'])" once="false">
  ::set{run.aff.ines += 1 when="run.seen.ines < run.day"}
  ::set{run.seen.ines = run.day}
  <match on="run.aff.ines">
    <when is="3..">
      @ines{code="0010" emotion="happy"}: I saved you the good chair. Don't tell anyone there's a good chair.
    </when>
    <otherwise>
      @ines{code="0020"}: We close at five.
    </otherwise>
  </match>
</beat>

<entry id="lighthouseUninvited" on="placeVisit" target="place.lighthouse" category="bark" when="holds('present', ['theo', 'lighthouse'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The lighthouse door is open a crack. Up on the gallery someone is sitting with his legs through the railings, watching the water. You don't go up. It isn't your night.
</entry>

<entry id="shopDark" on="placeVisit" target="place.shop" category="bark" when="!holds('present', ['pell', 'shop'])">
  @narrator{code="0010"}: The shop is dark. A card in the window: GONE TO THE WALK. BACK WHEN THE TIDE IS.
</entry>
